.TH BIGINTFACTORIAL 3 "2026-09-25" "BigNums 3" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigIntFactorial \- compute an exact factorial
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <bignums.h>

int bigIntFactorial(BigInt *result, uint32_t n);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Computes uint32_t n factorial by repeated scalar multiplication. Both 0! and
1! are one. The initialized output grows dynamically and is replaced only on
success. The loop terminates correctly even at the uint32_t counter boundary.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0, -1 for allocation failure, or INT_MAX for an unrepresentable size.
Errors leave the previous output unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
